100 MB     |         0.0196 s |     5104.65 MB/s |        0.0231 s |    4324.14 MB/s
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Key Findings:
1. Shared memory avoids kernel buffer double-copying, achieving significantly higher throughput.
2. Pipes require user->kernel and kernel->user copies, plus context switches on buffer full/empty.
3. For streaming weather telemetry (< few KB/s), pipes provide simple implicit synchronization (EOF on close).
